-- Bright water model with Adsorption depending on temperature 
-- Bright WaterTM Polymer injection
-- And its effect in solving thief zone issues 
-- Simple "2D" model with 1 INJ and 1 PROD well
-- April 2013
-- Keywords specific for Bright WaterTM: 
-- PLYTRRF
-- PLYKRRF
-- PLYATEMP
-- PLYADS

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
----------------------------- RUNSPEC SECTION -----------------------------
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

RUNSPEC     ==============================================================

TITLE
Bright water model with Adsorption depending on temperature

-- Reservoir dimension 50*3*5, surrounding by 1 block thick layer in all directions of 0 permeability 
-- to simulate the heat flow form the surrounding
DIMENS
  52 5 7 /

OIL

WATER

GAS

POLYMER

BRINE

UNIFIN
UNIFOUT

FIELD

TABDIMS
    2    1   40   20  1   20 /

START
   1 'MAY' 1990  /

NSTACK
    50 /

MESSAGES
3* 10000 5* 10000 /

TEMP


---------------------------------------------------------------------------
----------------------------- GRID SECTION --------------------------------
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GRID      ==============================================================

GRIDFILE
 1 1 /

INIT

TOPS
260*3790 /
DX
   1820*20 /
DY
   1820*20 /
DZ
   1820*10 /


-- Porosity of the outer layer 0.01 %  
EQUALS
PORO 0.01/
/
-- Porosity of the permeable reservoir 20 %
MULTIPLY
PORO 20 2 51 2 4 2 6 /
/

-- Definition of the 0 permeability layer
PERMX 
1820*0/
PERMY 
1820*0/
PERMZ 
1820*0/

--Definition of the thief zone in the x-direction (2 block thick)
BOX 
2 51 2 4 2 6 /  
PERMX
300*50
150*1000    -- Thief zone
300*50 /

COPY
PERMX PERMY /
PERMX PERMZ /
/
MULTIPLY
PERMZ .1 /
/
ENDBOX

THCONR
1820*25/


